# Line endings: LF in the repository AND in every checkout, on every OS. Git for Windows defaults
# to core.autocrlf=true, which checks text files out with CRLF unless this file says otherwise, and
# a hook, check or gate script with CRLF fails in sh (`$'\r': command not found`). WSL2 and macOS
# need nothing; the rule makes a checkout from Windows tools safe too. Add your own lines BELOW
# these: the last matching line wins. Held by .claude/checks/line-endings.sh.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary types: never converted, never diffed as text (text=auto detects most; these are certain).
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
